          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Based on your Checkpoint A analysis of the Campus Supply Desk application, I recommend the following three improvements:\n\n1. Prevent Duplicate Inventory Restoration During Order Cancellation\n\nAdd protection to ensure that an order can only be cancelled once. When an order is cancelled, its reserved inventory should be restored exactly once. Repeated cancellation attempts should be rejected or handled without changing stock again. This prevents inventory counts from becoming inaccurate and protects the application from inconsistent order state.\n\n2. Make JSON State Saves Atomic\n\nImprove the JSON persistence process so that updates are written to a temporary file first and only replace the existing save file after the write succeeds. This reduces the risk of leaving the application's saved order and inventory data partially written or corrupted if the process is interrupted or a write fails.\n\n3. Strengthen CR-01 Express Delivery Regression Testing\n\nAdd a regression test verifying that the fixed $12.00 Express Delivery fee remains separate from the student discount and is never reduced or waived. This ensures that future changes to the order processing logic do not inadvertently affect the delivery fee calculation, maintaining consistent pricing for express deliveries."
            ]
          },
